{
  "about": [
    "Shrink order of a pool, shared by every implementation that has a pool policy.",
    "A case gives the pool's members, the growth dials in progress (dialing, numbered 0 for the oldest to dialing-1 for the newest) and the decision: count, and retire, the keys the decision names.",
    "The pool's size is the members and dialing together. While it is above count, growth dials are cancelled first, newest first, then members close: those named in retire first, then the longest idle, ties broken by the fewest pipes, then the least age, then the highest key.",
    "expect lists the dials cancelled (by number, in order) and the keys closed (in order). An implementation whose pool reports dialing 0 passes the cases with dialing 0 only."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no-dialing-longest-idle-first",
      "members": [
        {
          "key": 1,
          "idle": 5,
          "pipes": 1,
          "age": 0
        },
        {
          "key": 2,
          "idle": 9,
          "pipes": 1,
          "age": 0
        },
        {
          "key": 3,
          "idle": 1,
          "pipes": 1,
          "age": 0
        }
      ],
      "dialing": 0,
      "decision": {
        "count": 2,
        "retire": []
      },
      "expect": {
        "cancel_dials": [],
        "close": [
          2
        ]
      }
    },
    {
